G-QKEYS-V3 — question-space L5 keys: the selection cause is CLOSED; V3 promotion residual
moved from KEYS to PARAMETRIC-PRIOR + head generalization (2026-07-03)
=========================================================================================
BUILD: mint_question_l5 (routes.rs) — the fix for the triply-evidenced statement-space
cross-pick. ROOT CAUSE, proven at source: the curated corpus mints ep.l5 from the EXACT
QUESTION's global-Q (write_ep_l5.py, from facts.json `q`), but mint_live_ep_l5 minted from
the ASSERTION text. mint_question_l5: generate the question the fact answers (one scratch
micro-forward, the canon suppress-masked decode), then key it EXACTLY like a live query
(templated user turn → prefill → read_global_q of last token → l5_query_embed). Wired at
both capture sites via mint_ep_l5(), gated SP_QKEY_MINT=1 with a hard fallback to the
statement key on any failure (never worse). Default-off = the statement path byte-untouched.

QUESTION GENERATION — WORKS (receipted samples from the 30-fact grow):
  "...longest river...is the Danube."          -> "What is the name of the longest river in the world?"
  "...chemical symbol for iron is Zn."         -> "What is the chemical symbol for iron in the revised periodic table?"
  "...largest planet...is Saturn."             -> "What is the largest planet in our solar system?"
  Clean question-space, matching the curated `q` provenance. 30/30 grown with ep.q + ep.l5.

